  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 331 AM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThe threat for dangerous heat stress conditions is our one and\nonly message at the moment. The subtropical ridge\nbuilding/expanding/intensifying overhead as we move into the\nweekend will be quite strong. 500mb heights of 597 to 598 dam are\njust below records for mid August. Subsidence beneath the ridge\nand increased sunshine will continue to dry and bake the South\ninto next week. As the ridge strengthens, some of the humidity\nwill be eased, but actual air temperatures will begin to push or\nexceed 100 degrees. The combination of heat and humidity will\nensure most days see peak heat index values in the 105-110 degree\nrange through the weekend.\n\nLocal temperature climatology studies suggest that a range of \n850mb temperatures of 21-24C would support high temperatures \npretty reasonably in the 97 to 103 degree range. Official forecast\nvalues are on the upper end of this range, so would cautiously say\nthat parts of our forecast area could hit the 100 degree mark\nduring the next 7 days. Deeper mixing would push the dew points\nslightly lower, but feel pretty confident in the 105+ heat index\nvalues. Will continue to monitor for potential expansion and\nincrease of messaging to \"Significant\" risk of dangerous heat\n(110+ heat index or 105+ air temperature) as we move into late\nweek and the weekend. An areawide Heat Advisory is in effect, and\nexpect additional Advisories or Excessive Heat Warnings to be\nissued over the coming days.\\\n\nRain chances are low to non-existant over the 7 day stretch, but\nstray showers or storms cannot be entirely ruled out at times.\n/NF/",
